; What the generated code calls in the executable besides the kernel's and XAM's imports and the runtime's replacements
; of game functions, which tools/moduledefs.py adds to the executable's exports with these.
; The runtime's (ppc_overrides.h):
?DOA4QueryTimeBase@@YA_KXZ
?GuestTrap@@YAXAEAUPPCContext@@PEAEII@Z
?GuestSwitchOutOfRange@@YAXII@Z
?XmaRegisterWrite@@YAXII@Z
PPCStoreMiss
PPCJmpBuf
; The C runtime's, which the shims in include/ declare: the executable's own (static) C runtime, so the generated code
; computes with the same functions as before the module, and follows _set_FMA3_enable (main.cpp) the same way. Each is
; exported from ModuleCrt_<name>, a jump to the C runtime's function (module/crt_exports.h), not by its name alone,
; which lld-link bound to a C++ overload of sqrt that called itself for negative inputs (ANALYSIS.md, Phase 6, The CPU
; fights' hang); tools/moduledefs.py refuses an export the executable's objects don't define by its name alone.
_setjmp=ModuleCrt__setjmp
longjmp=ModuleCrt_longjmp
memcpy=ModuleCrt_memcpy
memset=ModuleCrt_memset
sqrt=ModuleCrt_sqrt
sqrtf=ModuleCrt_sqrtf
fma=ModuleCrt_fma
exp2f=ModuleCrt_exp2f
log2f=ModuleCrt_log2f
